A 50 Hz, 275 kV line of length 400 km has the following parameters:
Resistance, \(R = 0.035\) Ω/km;
Inductance, \(L = 1\) mH/km;
Capacitance, \(C = 0.01\) μF/km;
The line is represented by the nominal-π model. With the magnitudes of the sending end and the receiving end voltages of the line (denoted by \(V_S\) and \(V_R\), respectively) maintained at 275 kV, the phase angle difference (θ) between \(V_S\) and \(V_R\) required for maximum possible active power to be delivered to the receiving end, in degree is _____________ (Round off to 2 decimal places).

